ed unhealthy. My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1 for a short time. I retried the same rollback and it finished in us-west and eu-west. All regions are now on v2.3.0. The service passes health checks and the error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is a SEV2 for checkout-api and covers the bad deploy, the rollback, the partial failure and the next steps. The request to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. It had already been created, so I didn't send it again, which would have paged on-call a second time.\n\n**Next steps (also noted in the incident):** find out why v2.3.1 is failing and what caused the orchestrator error before anyone redeploys v2.3.x.", "type": "text"}]}]}